[size=6][color=#FFD600][b]Body Change NG v1.3.5[/b][/color][/size]
[hr]
[size=4][color=#19D8FF][b]Easier NPC distribution[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Added a Distribution conditions button to Body Presets, Body Skins, Futanari Skin, and Overlays. Open existing rules directly without selecting items or creating a new rule first.
[*]Manage rules across four tabs and use Edit items to add or remove candidates from an existing rule. The item picker includes search, Select all, and Clear selection.
[*]Added search to the plugin, race, faction, keyword, and class dropdowns. Find entries by name, EditorID, plugin, or FormID, with improved EditorID display for unnamed factions.
[*]Moved the final Save button next to Close and show its result inside the conditions window. Improved feature labels and Korean, English, and Chinese UI text.
[*]Automatic NPC previews now select human or elf races, excluding Khajiit and Argonians. This affects preview selection only, not actual distribution rules. Removed repeated notifications when checking items that cannot be previewed.
[/list]
[hr]
[size=4][color=#19D8FF][b]Body and skin fixes[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Fixed player-face skins sometimes looking different in preview and after confirmation. Cancelling restores the original appearance, and unconfirmed face changes are kept out of saves.
[*]Preserved the default UBE RFAOS/wet effect links during skin changes and fixed unwanted droplets appearing only after selecting a skin. Cache files referenced by older saves are retained.
[*]Improved native UBE and TRX UBE futanari addon detection, showing skins for the matching addon. Existing CBBE 3BA TRX/ERF handling is preserved.
[*]Added a targeted compatibility fix for inflated shapes after equipping outfits with a specific RaceMenu DLL bundled with UBE SE on Skyrim 1.5.97. Preset calculations, breast/nipple correction values, and randomization recipes are unchanged.
[/list]
[hr]
[size=4][color=#19D8FF][b]Updating[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Fully exit the game before replacing the mod, then restart. Keep your settings, distribution rules, favorites, skin packs, and texture caches. No new game or save cleaning is required; supported game versions are unchanged.
[/list]
